    <string name="about">About</string>
    <string name="about_text">Soft Landing %1$s. Everything stays on the phone; only barcodes and searches go to Open Food Facts. Barcode scanning and label reading run on the phone with Google ML Kit. Fonts: Prata, Manrope, Caveat (SIL OFL).</string>
    <string name="about_foods">Foods on the phone</string>
    <string name="source">Source code</string>
    <string name="n_channel">Evening reminder</string>
    <string name="n_fog_t">The balloon is flying in fog</string>
    <string name="n_fog_b">Nothing written down today. Even a rough note is better than fog.</string>
    <string name="n_light_t">The balloon is still high</string>
    <string name="n_light_b">Don\'t forget dinner: without it the balloon drifts past the meadow.</string>
    <string name="ob_1">Every day is a balloon flight to the next village.</string>
    <string name="ob_1b">In the morning the balloon is light and high. Each thing you eat is ballast, and the balloon comes down. The aim is to land softly on the meadow by evening: your daily norm, give or take. Too much and you come down early in a field; too little and the wind carries you past. Soft landings move you along the route, and every village gives a recipe.</string>
    <string name="ob_2">Who\'s flying?</string>
    <string name="ob_2b">This is enough to work out the norm. Everything stays on the phone.</string>
    <string name="ob_3">Your meadow</string>
    <string name="ob_3b">The norm is worked out from your profile. It changes in settings at any time.</string>
    <string name="ob_3c">Writing things down is quick: scan a barcode, type “buckwheat 200, 2 eggs” in one line, or repeat yesterday\'s breakfast in one tap.</string>
    <string name="ob_3d">Two days a month can be fairs: birthdays and holidays don\'t count and don\'t break the streak.</string>
    <string name="ob_start">Take off</string>
